WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:04.060
The Mighty Ducks might never have made it
to the screen if weren't for Wayne Gretzky's

00:00:04.060 --> 00:00:09.230
trade to the LA Kings in 1988, a move that
sparked an increased interest in ice hockey

00:00:09.230 --> 00:00:13.550
throughout Los Angeles — and didn't go unnoticed
by Hollywood execs.

00:00:13.550 --> 00:00:17.930
Steven Brill's script about a down-and-out
lawyer taking over a useless pee-wee team

00:00:17.930 --> 00:00:22.390
was picked up by Disney, and the Mouse House
quickly set about preparing sequels after

00:00:22.390 --> 00:00:25.570
the box office success of the 1992 original.

00:00:25.570 --> 00:00:30.400
Coach Gordon Bombay and his ragtag roster
of players triple-deked their way into pop

00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:31.460
culture history.

00:00:31.460 --> 00:00:33.739
"Ducks never say die.

00:00:33.739 --> 00:00:35.210
Ever seen a duck fight?

00:00:35.210 --> 00:00:36.210
No way.

00:00:36.210 --> 00:00:37.210
Why?

00:00:37.210 --> 00:00:38.769
'Cause the other animals are afraid"

00:00:38.769 --> 00:00:43.820
But you can't play pee-wee forever, and Bombay's
ducklings are now all grown up — and not

00:00:43.820 --> 00:00:47.620
all of them found Hollywood success after
leaving the nest.

00:00:47.620 --> 00:00:49.530
Emilio Estevez

00:00:49.530 --> 00:00:54.539
The role of Gordon Bombay allowed Emilio Estevez
to shake off the Brat Pack tag he carried

00:00:54.539 --> 00:00:55.760
throughout the '80s.

00:00:55.760 --> 00:01:00.539
He'd already attempted to move away from coming-of-age
dramedies with his turn as Billy the Kid in

00:01:00.539 --> 00:01:04.890
the Young Guns movies, though Bombay was his
first real grown-up character.

00:01:04.890 --> 00:01:09.960
He carried on acting into the late '90s and
early '00s, but now spends much of his time

00:01:09.960 --> 00:01:11.240
writing and directing.

00:01:11.240 --> 00:01:16.230
He still holds Gordon Bombay close to his
heart, however, which he proved in 2015 when

00:01:16.230 --> 00:01:21.030
he live-tweeted support for the Anaheim Ducks
during their playoff showdown with the Chicago

00:01:21.030 --> 00:01:22.190
Blackhawks.

00:01:22.190 --> 00:01:23.899
Joshua Jackson

00:01:23.899 --> 00:01:28.409
The part of championship-winning penalty scorer
Charlie Conway was originally supposed to

00:01:28.409 --> 00:01:32.880
be played by a young Jake Gyllenhaal, who
was offered the part on the back of his performance

00:01:32.880 --> 00:01:36.310
as Billy Crystal's son 1991's City Slickers.

00:01:36.310 --> 00:01:40.600
Joshua Jackson stepped in when Jake couldn't
take it, which kickstarted a career that's

00:01:40.600 --> 00:01:45.170
grown to include five-season stints on Dawson's
Creek and Fringe.

00:01:45.170 --> 00:01:50.499
Jackson made his transition from movies to
TV after taking his final bow as Charlie in

00:01:50.499 --> 00:01:55.979
1996's Mighty Ducks threequel, D3, and he
remains a man of the small screen today, starring

00:01:55.979 --> 00:01:58.270
in Showtime's The Affair.

00:01:58.270 --> 00:01:59.909
Elden Henson

00:01:59.909 --> 00:02:04.460
It's hard to believe Matt Murdock's loveable
sidekick Foggy Nelson is the same guy that

00:02:04.460 --> 00:02:06.840
played hulking enforcer Fulton Reed.

00:02:06.840 --> 00:02:10.580
Elden Henson made his first appearance in
The Mighty Ducks when members of the team

00:02:10.580 --> 00:02:15.020
were cornered by players from their rival
team the Hawks, dispatching the bullies with

00:02:15.020 --> 00:02:16.020
ease.

00:02:16.020 --> 00:02:20.000
Henson went on to be a key member of the team
and the cast over the course of the three

00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:21.000
movies.

00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:24.950
But when the Ducks disbanded, he struggled
to make an impact in the show biz industry,

00:02:24.950 --> 00:02:28.830
resorting to supporting parts in such films
as The Butterfly Effect.

00:02:28.830 --> 00:02:32.730
Henson's fortunes have a taken a turn for
the better over recent years — not only

00:02:32.730 --> 00:02:36.751
on the big screen, when he played the part
of Pollux in the two-part Hunger Games finale,

00:02:36.751 --> 00:02:38.790
but on television, too.

00:02:38.790 --> 00:02:43.670
He's portrayed well-meaning lawyer Foggy in
Netflix's Daredevil, as well as in the team-up

00:02:43.670 --> 00:02:46.090
series The Defenders.

00:02:46.090 --> 00:02:47.350
Shaun Weiss

00:02:47.350 --> 00:02:52.910
Before making his film debut in The Mighty
Ducks, Shaun Weiss worked on several TV shows,

00:02:52.910 --> 00:02:55.450
including an early appearance on The Cosby
Show.

00:02:55.450 --> 00:03:00.900
By 1992, he'd grown into a big-boned 14-year-old
and was considered a perfect fit for the role

00:03:00.900 --> 00:03:03.060
of goalie Greg Goldberg.

00:03:03.060 --> 00:03:06.400
"Ah I smell something."

00:03:06.400 --> 00:03:08.160
"Goldberg!"

00:03:08.160 --> 00:03:12.520
He went on to portray the flatulent goalie
in the Ducks sequels, taking time off between

00:03:12.520 --> 00:03:18.060
them to star in early Ben Stiller comedy Heavyweights,
a film that went on to amass a cult following

00:03:18.060 --> 00:03:19.120
of its own.

00:03:19.120 --> 00:03:24.090
Weiss saw the '90s out with a four-episode
stint on Judd Apatow's Freaks and Geeks — though

00:03:24.090 --> 00:03:28.561
the next decade wasn't kind to him, with his
most significant appearance in a feature film

00:03:28.561 --> 00:03:33.120
coming as the unnamed bus driver in 2008's
Drillbit Taylor.

00:03:33.120 --> 00:03:34.840
Matt Doherty

00:03:34.840 --> 00:03:38.940
After taking the part of Lester Averman in
the Mighty Ducks movies, Matt Doherty got

00:03:38.940 --> 00:03:43.110
another '90s classic on his resume in So I
Married an Axe Murderer.

00:03:43.110 --> 00:03:47.520
As he approached adulthood, roles started
to dry up for Doherty, and he walked the tightrope

00:03:47.520 --> 00:03:49.880
between supporting actor and extra.

00:03:49.880 --> 00:03:54.400
In recent years, he's turned to TV movies
and found some success on the sci-fi small

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:56.120
screen scene.

00:03:56.120 --> 00:03:57.740
Garette Henson

00:03:57.740 --> 00:04:02.390
This young star got off to a flying start
with his movie career, appearing in ten feature

00:04:02.390 --> 00:04:04.210
films over a six-year period.

00:04:04.210 --> 00:04:08.940
He made his bow in Arachnophobia, for example,
but Garette Henson is perhaps best remembered

00:04:08.940 --> 00:04:11.680
as Guy Germaine from The Mighty Ducks movies.

00:04:11.680 --> 00:04:15.930
While he admits to enjoying a chat about the
Ducks today, being associated with the films

00:04:15.930 --> 00:04:18.459
started to wear thin towards the end of the
decade.

00:04:18.459 --> 00:04:22.480
He ultimately stepped away from acting to
pursue college and made a brief return to

00:04:22.480 --> 00:04:27.020
the biz in 2007 when he played a prisoner
in The Mannsfield 12.

00:04:27.020 --> 00:04:30.050
He's now busy working behind the lens.

00:04:30.050 --> 00:04:31.760
Danny Tamberelli

00:04:31.760 --> 00:04:36.420
Italian-American actor and musician Danny
Tamberelli played the role of defenseman Tommy

00:04:36.420 --> 00:04:40.650
Duncan in The Mighty Ducks, though he didn't
return for either of the sequels.

00:04:40.650 --> 00:04:45.000
Instead, Tamberelli opted to take on the role
of Little Pete Wrigley in Nickelodeon's The

00:04:45.000 --> 00:04:48.690
Adventures of Pete and Pete, the role that
he's still best remembered for.

00:04:48.690 --> 00:04:53.140
The kids' network added him to the cast of
their slimy game show Figure It Out and their

00:04:53.140 --> 00:04:57.820
live sketch comedy All That in the late '90s,
though he departed from Nickelodeon at the

00:04:57.820 --> 00:05:01.880
turn of the millennium and transitioned into
voice work, music, and comedy.

00:05:01.880 --> 00:05:05.750
Nowadays Tamberelli fronts Brooklyn-based
rock band Jounce.

00:05:05.750 --> 00:05:07.930
Jussie Smollett

00:05:07.930 --> 00:05:12.410
Justin "Jussie" Smollett recently pulled off
a comeback worthy of the Mighty Ducks, turning

00:05:12.410 --> 00:05:16.520
his fading career around and putting himself
firmly back on the Hollywood map.

00:05:16.520 --> 00:05:20.490
Smollett appeared in the first Ducks movie
but didn't reprise the role of Terry Hall

00:05:20.490 --> 00:05:25.260
in either sequel, and it wasn't until the
2010s, when landed a career-making role in

00:05:25.260 --> 00:05:28.610
Fox's hit series Empire that things got back
on track.

00:05:28.610 --> 00:05:33.800
Thanks to his compelling work on the celebrated
series, Ridley Scott cast him in his Prometheus

00:05:33.800 --> 00:05:37.560
sequel Alien: Covenant and he's well on his
way to the top.

00:05:37.560 --> 00:05:38.930
Vincent Larusso

00:05:38.930 --> 00:05:43.170
When we first meet Adam Banks in The Mighty
Ducks, he's the star player for the Ducks'

00:05:43.170 --> 00:05:47.240
rival team, who had to change squads due to
his fudged home address.

00:05:47.240 --> 00:05:51.450
He was an unlikely hero for the Ducks in the
end, and Vincent Larusso portrayed Banks in

00:05:51.450 --> 00:05:53.370
all three Mighty Ducks movies.

00:05:53.370 --> 00:05:57.480
Larusso made a brief and unexpected return
to the big screen when he portrayed the bank

00:05:57.480 --> 00:06:02.340
robber in the 2008 spoof Superhero Movie,
though that remains his last credit of any

00:06:02.340 --> 00:06:03.340
note.

00:06:03.340 --> 00:06:07.520
Today, the former Duck works as an inventory
controller for the hospitality chain Soho

00:06:07.520 --> 00:06:08.930
House.

00:06:08.930 --> 00:06:10.770
Brandon Adams

00:06:10.770 --> 00:06:14.860
Otherwise known as Jesse Hall in the first
two Mighty Ducks movies, Brandon Adams was

00:06:14.860 --> 00:06:19.510
exposed to the world of acting as a toddler
when he appeared in a number of commercials.

00:06:19.510 --> 00:06:24.170
But his big break came when he was cast as
Zeke "Baby Bad" Michael in Michael Jackson's

00:06:24.170 --> 00:06:25.170
Moonwalker.

00:06:25.170 --> 00:06:28.790
He went on to work with Wes Craven in The
People Under the Stairs before nabbing the

00:06:28.790 --> 00:06:30.169
Mighty Ducks role.

00:06:30.169 --> 00:06:34.139
Adams always had one foot in film while the
other remained in television, however, and

00:06:34.139 --> 00:06:37.790
he started to lean more heavily on the latter
as his career progressed.

00:06:37.790 --> 00:06:42.580
He has some genuine '90s classics to his name,
including The Sandlot.

00:06:42.580 --> 00:06:44.520
Marguerite Moreau

00:06:44.520 --> 00:06:48.730
As Connie in The Mighty Ducks, Marguerite
Moreau may have inspired a lot of young girls

00:06:48.730 --> 00:06:51.480
to break down gender norms and hit the ice.

00:06:51.480 --> 00:06:57.010
The actress seemed to grow up pretty quickly
after the Mighty Ducks trilogy ended in 1996,

00:06:57.010 --> 00:07:01.610
appearing as camp counselor Katie in Wet Hot
American Summer a short five years later.

00:07:01.610 --> 00:07:04.870
A major role in Queen of the Damned followed
soon after.

00:07:04.870 --> 00:07:09.090
But while she continued to make regular movie
appearances throughout the '00s, the parts

00:07:09.090 --> 00:07:14.100
she was offered became increasingly unfulfilling
and she turned her attention to television.

00:07:14.100 --> 00:07:18.919
Moreau has plied her trade in small-screen
classics such as Smallville, Parenthood, and

00:07:18.919 --> 00:07:24.400
Mad Men and also reprised the role of Katie
in 2015 when she reunited with her Wet Hot

00:07:24.400 --> 00:07:29.650
American Summer castmates for Netflix's prequel
series First Day of Camp.

00:07:29.650 --> 00:07:31.340
J.D. Daniels

00:07:31.340 --> 00:07:36.180
Even though he was a prolific child actor
in the 1990s, J.D. Daniels did not come back

00:07:36.180 --> 00:07:40.830
to reprise the role of Peter Mark in either
of the Mighty Ducks sequels and instead went

00:07:40.830 --> 00:07:44.520
on to win a number of new roles across a variety
of genres.

00:07:44.520 --> 00:07:48.550
Like some of his Ducks colleagues, Daniels
moved into voiceover work, and although he

00:07:48.550 --> 00:07:53.920
hasn't notched up an acting credit in almost
a decade, Daniels remains active in the industry,

00:07:53.920 --> 00:07:57.350
currently working for the Actors' Equity Association.

00:07:57.350 --> 00:07:58.919
Aaron Schwartz

00:07:58.919 --> 00:08:03.550
Practically unrecognizable today, the broad
and bearded Aaron Schwartz has come a long

00:08:03.550 --> 00:08:07.660
way since playing chubby prankster Dave Karp
in the first Mighty Ducks.

00:08:07.660 --> 00:08:12.130
He joined up with fellow Duck Danny Tamberelli
for an eight-episode stint on The Adventures

00:08:12.130 --> 00:08:17.320
of Pete and Pete, then teamed up with another
former castmate, Shaun Weiss, for Judd Apatow's

00:08:17.320 --> 00:08:18.320
Heavyweights.

00:08:18.320 --> 00:08:22.610
When the formerly heavyset Schwartz reappeared
after a 15-year absence from the industry

00:08:22.610 --> 00:08:26.910
in the CW's Gossip Girl, he'd grown into a
primetime-worthy hunk.

00:08:26.910 --> 00:08:32.169
He'll join the Marvel Cinematic Universe in
2017 when he takes on the role of Young Ego

00:08:32.169 --> 00:08:36.889
in Guardians of the Galaxy Vol. 2, a younger
version of Kurt Russell's character.

00:08:36.889 --> 00:08:41.450
"Just when you think they're about to break
apart, ducks fly together!"

00:08:41.450 --> 00:08:44.290
"Ducks, ducks, ducks, ducks!"

00:08:44.290 --> 00:08:45.439
Thanks for watching!

00:08:45.439 --> 00:08:48.540
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:08:48.540 --> 00:08:51.129
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

